  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, in the same format as the earlier entries:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n- **Version and date:** these come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files.\n- **Breaking change:** ACME-421 has a `!` in `merged_prs.txt`, so I labelled it **BREAKING** and put it first so users who rely on `--legacy` see it.\n- **Order:** the new feature and the upload retry come next, then the two bug fixes.\n- **Authors:** I left out the `@mira`-style author names because earlier entries don't include them. I can add them if you want credits.\n\n**Decision for you:** if this project follows semantic versioning, removing `--legacy` normally calls for a major version bump (3.0.0), not 2.4.0. I didn't change the version, because the flag was already deprecated and your project may handle that differently. If you want to bump it, I'll update both `VERSION` and the notes.",
